    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d220">

                <pb facs="0300" n="202" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg202"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">574.D7/1647: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hsieh Chieh-shih to the Secretary of
                        State</hi><anchor n="25" xml:id="d220-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Changchun</hi></placeName>, [<date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-08-19">August 19, 1932</date>].<lb/>[Received August 19—10:49
                        a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I had the honor in my telegram addressed to Your Excellency, dated April
                        23,<anchor n="26" xml:id="d220-f2"/> to express the desire of the Government
                    of the State <pb facs="0301" n="203" xml:id="pg203"/> of Manchuria to adhere to
                    the International Radio Telegraphic Convention<anchor n="27" xml:id="d220-f3"/>
                    and to regulations annexed thereto.</p>
                <p>I now respectfully ask that you will be good enough to take prompt action in the
                    matter requested in the said telegraphic communication.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hsieh Chieh-shih</hi></signed><lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d220-f1" n="25" type="source" xml:id="d220-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was filed without acknowledgment.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d220-f2" n="26" xml:id="d220-f2-content">
